course: dictionary
lesson: 14497
title: Pectoral: a word about the chest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pectoral is an adjective that means "of or on the chest". The chest is the front of your body, between your neck and your belly. When you see pectoral muscles, the word tells you the muscles are on your chest.
explain: «Sam did ten push-ups to make his pectoral muscles stronger.» Push-ups use your arms and chest, so the clues are push-ups and stronger. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Sam did ten push-ups to make his chest muscles stronger" still makes sense, so chest is right.
explain: Pectoral can also be a noun, and gym users often shorten it to «pecs», which is informal. Pectoral has another meaning too: a pectoral fin is one of the pair of fins on the sides of a fish, just behind the head. The clues around the word show which meaning you need.
explain: «The goldfish used its pectoral fins to steer around the rock.» Fins and steer tell you this is about a fish, so pectoral means on the side of the fish. When the clues are not enough, a dictionary can confirm the meaning.
fact: Pectoral means of or on the chest.
fact: Pectoral can be an adjective, as in «pectoral muscles», or a noun, as in «a pectoral».
fact: Pectoral muscles move your arms and shoulders, and push-ups make them stronger.
fact: «Pecs» is an informal, everyday short name for the pectoral muscles.
fact: A pectoral fin is one of the pair of fins on the sides of a fish, just behind the head, used to steer and stop.
exercise: «Sam did ten push-ups to make his pectoral muscles stronger.» What does pectoral mean here? | A type of bread | *Of or on the chest | Of or on the legs | Very fast
exercise: «The goldfish used its pectoral fins to steer around the rock.» Where are pectoral fins on a fish? | *On the sides, just behind the head | Under the water | On the tail | Inside the mouth
exercise: Ben says, «My pecs ache after the gym.» What does pecs mean? | *The pectoral muscles of the chest | Pencils | A type of fish | Very tired feet
test: «The bishop wore a pectoral cross on a chain.» Where did the bishop wear the cross? | On the foot | *On the chest | In the hand | On the head
test: «Push-ups can make your pectoral muscles stronger.» What do push-ups help? | Make your legs longer | Make your hair grow faster | *Make the chest muscles stronger | Make fish swim faster
exam: Which word means "of or on the chest"? | tail | fin | *pectoral | fish
